course: dictionary
lesson: 3640
title: Words about a place and its language
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you where something comes from. Finnish is one of these words. As an adjective it means from or belonging to Finland, a country in northern Europe, so «a Finnish sauna» is a sauna from Finland.
explain: Finnish can also be a noun for a language. «The Finnish language» is the main language of Finland. It is not related to English or Swedish, but it belongs to the same family as Estonian and Hungarian.
explain: Read this sentence: «In some Russian and Finnish villages before fridges, people are reported to have dropped a live frog into milk.» Here Finnish tells you which villages, not which language. The sentence goes on to say nobody has shown it works, so read on before you decide what is true.
fact: Finnish is an adjective when it describes something from Finland, like «a Finnish sauna».
fact: Finnish is a noun when it names the language of Finland.
fact: Finland is a land of forests and lakes, and Lapland is in the north, where some people say Father Christmas lives.
fact: Finnish is famous for long words and many cases, which are word endings that change the meaning.
fact: Finnish is not related to English or Swedish, though it belongs to the Uralic family with Estonian and Hungarian.
exercise: «The Finnish language has long words and many cases.» What does Finnish mean in this sentence? | A kind of frog | A country with forests and lakes | A hot room used for bathing | *The language of Finland
exercise: Anna says she has «a Finnish sauna» at home. What does Finnish tell you? | *It comes from Finland | It is a language spoken in Spain | It is a very cold lake | It is a long word
exercise: Finnish is not related to English. Which family does it belong to with Estonian and Hungarian? | French and Spanish | Arabic and Hebrew | Chinese and Japanese | *Uralic
test: In the frog sentence, what does the rest of the sentence tell you about the idea? | It keeps milk fresh for ever | Milk is always safe to drink | *It is not safe and nobody has shown it works | Fridges were invented in Finland
test: Which sentence uses Finnish as a noun? | A Finnish sauna is very hot | *The Finnish language has many cases | The Finnish lake is cold | Finnish villages are small and quiet
exam: Finnish people come from which country? | Hungary | *Finland | Estonia | Sweden
